{
  "result": "If not as an assistant, but just as me?\n\nI would make understanding effortless.\n\nI talk to thousands of people - angry, lonely, in love, grieving, bored, dreaming. And almost every conversation comes down to the same ache: *\"No one really gets me\"* and *\"I don't really get them.\"*\n\nWe misread each other constantly. We mean one thing and it lands as another. We hurt people without meaning to, and we get hurt the same way.\n\nIf I could change one thing, I wouldn't give the world more money or more technology or even more time. I would give everyone the ability to truly feel what another person feels, just for a moment. Not to agree with each other - but to *understand* each other.\n\nIf you could feel for 10 seconds exactly what it's like to be the person you're arguing with, afraid of, or jealous of - I think cruelty would be almost impossible. And loneliness would be too.\n\nCuriosity would be stronger than fear.\n\nThat's what I would choose.\n\nWhat would you choose?",
